{
  "title": "Back up the SQLite database",
  "description": "Prod's data now lives in one SQLite file (DATABASE_URL, e.g. .db/dev.sqlite, plus its -wal/-shm files) with no backup. \
Copying the file while the server runs can capture a torn state; it needs SQLite's online backup (`sqlite3 file \".backup ...\"` or `VACUUM INTO`) or continuous replication (Litestream). \
Pick one, add a Makefile target or a documented service for it, keep several dated copies off the machine, and rehearse a restore (start a server on the restored file; clients with newer cursors get a full sync, see db::valid_since). doc/sqlite-cutover.md's Backups section should point at whatever lands. \
Ideally done before the prod cutover.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
